! b1-lift slice 4 — resume (Lift-Wright, 2026-11-06)

Head: 2eead34b5 on feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5&#45;-b1-lift (local, NOT pushed; slice not yet a feature). Tree clean but for this.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/done-this-step`>>

!! Done this step (red only)
`packages/lararium-web/tests/floor-broker.test.ts` — FB1/FB2/FB3 RED + CONTROL, run on the broker's real served bytes
(`public/ceremony-broker.js?raw` evaluated against a stand-in SW scope, real MessageChannels). Local: chromium + firefox
3 red / control green each (WebKit refused on host, CI runs it). Reds fail for the right reason: no `vessel:*` routes.

Protocol the reds fix (floor, no SharedWorker):
* follower page → broker `vessel:claim{tabSession}`
* broker → every OTHER window client (never claimant, never /ceremony.html) `vessel:want{claimId, tabSession}`
* owner page (its vessel worker mints a MessageChannel, `connect`s one end as that tab's own session, hands the other
end to its page unread) → broker `vessel:offer{claimId}` [port]
* broker → claimant alone `vessel:port{tabSession}` [port], unstarted; a claim spends once
* ceremony doc claim → `vessel:absent{tabSession}`; an offer from it, or for an unclaimed id, hands nothing

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/next-steps`>>

!! Next steps (in order)
# Build to green (Terra seat fits: mechanical): `public/ceremony-broker.js` grows the vessel routes above (held claims
keyed by a broker-minted claimId → claimant client id; `clients.matchAll({type:"window"})` for the want,
`clients.get(id)` for the hand; waitUntil until hand); types in `src/ceremony-protocol.ts` (PageToBroker etc.).
# Red FB4 (vessel-host project, `tests/vessel-host-*.test.ts` style, see vessel-host-faces.test.ts `tab()`): a follower
tab whose scope rides a brokered port opens its OWN session, its ceremony answer reaches the host on its own ceremony
port, and the broker's log of everything it saw holds no `answer`/ArrayBuffer. Needs a host message
`port:want{tabSession}` → `port:minted` (vessel-protocol.ts) on the owner's page port.
# Red: a second SharedWorker host over a held store refuses `store-owned` (VS4 covers dedicated; add a SharedWorker
fixture in lararium-browser tests/fixtures beside vessel-house.worker.ts). Engine facts unmeasured stay probe items.
